# The terminal talks only to same-origin paths (P16-4): /ws, /api, /health and /market. In
# production Caddy serves them beside the page; under `npm run dev` the Vite dev server proxies
# them to the venue at EXCHANGE_BACKEND_URL (default http://localhost:8080). To use a venue on
# another port, set it in the shell or in .env.local, for example:
#   EXCHANGE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:18080
# VITE_WS_URL is an optional override of the WebSocket endpoint and is unset by default, so no
# backend host is baked into a build. Set it in .env.local only, for example:
#   VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:18080/ws
#
# The ignition price (the header's Open) comes from the venue's GET /market/ignition (P16-3).
# The Alpaca credentials are backend settings: ALPACA_KEY_ID and ALPACA_SECRET_KEY in the
# venue's environment (Windows user scope locally, credo.env on the server). Nothing here or in
# vite.config.ts reads them. The bots still read them from .env.local until P16-5.
